@seb-jean I’ve played with a `Role` entity, the `EntityType`, and the default storage (Session), and I encountered the following runtime exception when moving back to the previous step:

>Entity of type "App\Entity\Role" passed to the choice field must be managed. Maybe you forget to persist it in the entity manager?

That happens during the choice value resolution, where the `IdReader` tries to get the ID value of the entity (first checking if the given entity is currently managed) but it fails in this case (as expected) because the entity object was retrieved from the session, not from the EM (which is fresh in the next request).

In this scenario, given the context, my recommendation is to provide the `choice_value` resolver directly:
```php
->add('role', EntityType::class, [
    'class' => Role::class,
    'choice_value' => fn (?Role $role) => $role?->id, // <-- resolving the choice value manually
])
```
I don’t think `FormFlow` (or its data storage) can handle this situation any better.

Once the `FormFlow` is finished, it's over, and you've full control over the following [doctrine recommendations](https://www.doctrine-project.org/projects/doctrine-orm/en/3.3/cookbook/entities-in-session.html), either by mapping your DTO back to entities or by reloading the related entities when necessary.

